      "title": "Facilities Operations Support",
      "description": "Dean College\nJob Posting: Facilities Operations Support Dean College \n\tJob Posting: Facilities Operations Support Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Facilities Operations Support Category: Administration/Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Facilities Locations: Franklin, MA Posted: Sep 21, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-Time Fiscal Year Position ID: 205030 Share About Dean College: Dean College is a private, residential New England college grounded in a culture and tradition that all students deserve the opportunity to discover and exceed their greatest aspirations. A personal and transformative community since 1865, Dean tirelessly inspires our students to unimagined heights through personalized support and integrated delivery of academic, co-curricular, and experiential learning. Our graduates are lifelong learners who thrive in their careers, embrace social responsibility, and demonstrate leadership. Recognized as a Top Regional College by U.S. News & World Report for fifteenth consecutive years and named a College of Distinction for eleven consecutive years, Dean serves more than 1,000 full-time students and offers over 50 academic programs and specializations, as well as a robust schedule of continuing studies and certificate programs throughout the year. Dean College is perfectly situated in Franklin, Massachusetts, which is conveniently located between Boston and Providence, Rhode Island, and is accessible to Boston by commuter rail. The Dean College/Franklin rail station is only a five-minute walk from campus. Approximately 90 percent of the College's student population lives on campus and Dean provides a supportive academic environment that thrives on hands-on engagement and exceptional teaching. This community-wide commitment of always going the extra mile for students is known as The Dean Difference. Outside of the classroom, students participate in 16 athletic teams and more than 40 on-campus groups and organizations. Ninety-six percent of our bachelor's degree students are employed or enrolled in graduate school within 12 months of graduation. Alumni are hard at work in top-ranked graduate programs and are employed by organizations such as Universal Studios, Dell Technologies, Liberty Mutual, Kraft Sports + Entertainment, the Boston Ballet, and more. What is The Dean Difference? The Dean Difference isn't any one thing. It's not a program or a professor. It's not a single class or a club. It's the way our academic support networks and community overlap, interweave, and magnify each other. Our difference unites us. It's our secret formula. It's the nucleus around which we orbit. It isn't one thing, it's everything. Job Description: The Facilities Operations Support position supports the daily operations of campus by providing essential logistical support for event setup, campus activities, and mailroom operations. The ideal candidate is proactive and dependable, able to work both independently and collaboratively. A primary responsibility of this role is coordinating the movement and delivery of furniture, equipment, packages, and mail across campus, while supporting event setup and other campus activities. This is a full-time, non-exempt position starting at $22.00-$23.00 per hour, commensurate with experience. The College also offers a comprehensive benefits package, including health insurance, retirement contributions, and generous paid time off. Position responsibilities include: Provide setup, breakdown, and logistical support for internal and external events. Provide mailroom support, including package delivery, post office pickups, package scanning, and mail distribution to students and campus offices. Receive, document, and inventory deliveries for campus departments, as needed. Operate laundry equipment to clean and prepare table coverings and linens for campus events. Assemble office furniture and chairs, as requested. Manage the inventory, condition, delivery, and relocation of furniture and equipment; perform routine maintenance and report damaged or malfunctioning items to Facilities Management. Support additional Facilities-related tasks and special projects, as assigned or required. Requirements: High school diploma or GED required. Ability to kneel, bend, and safely lift or move furniture and equipment weighing up to 50 lbs. Valid Massachusetts driver's license required. Ability to work independently with minimal supervision while maintaining a strong commitment to teamwork and collaboration. Flexibility to work evenings, weekends, and overtime as needed to support campus events, programs, and daily operations. Work hours may be adjusted as needed to support special events and programs. Strong customer service skills with the ability to follow through and complete tasks efficiently. Demonstrated reliability, punctuality, and effective verbal and written communication skills. Familiarity with, or willingness to learn, basic Microsoft Office applications, including Outlook, Excel, and Word. Additional Information: Dean College is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate against applicants or employees on the basis of race, color, religion, religious creed, national or ethnic origin, ancestry, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, or any other status protected by applicable law. This commitment applies to all employment practices, including recruitment, hiring, promotion, compensation, benefits, professional development, continuation of employment, and other terms and conditions of employment. The College prohibits discrimination, harassment, and retaliation in violation of applicable law or College policy. Dean College is committed to maintaining a welcoming and respectful workplace and to providing equal opportunity to all qualified applicants and employees. Application Instructions: Please submit your Resume/CV, Cover Letter, all unofficial transcripts; and contact information of three references. (PLEASE NOTE: Applications that are incomplete will not be considered). Note: After submitting your resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your Cover Letter and any additional documents. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Dean College Careers Account to check your completed application or upload additional documents. URL: www.dean.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Dean College 99 Main Street, Franklin MA 02038"
