      "title": "Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice",
      "description": "Dean College\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice Dean College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Liberal Arts and Sciences Locations: Franklin, MA Posted: Aug 17, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-Time Academic Year Position ID: 203779 Share About Dean College: Dean College is a private, residential New England college grounded in a culture and tradition that all students deserve the opportunity to discover and exceed their greatest aspirations. A personal and transformative community since 1865, Dean tirelessly inspires our students to unimagined heights through personalized support and integrated delivery of academic, co-curricular, and experiential learning. Our graduates are lifelong learners who thrive in their careers, embrace social responsibility, and demonstrate leadership. Recognized as a Top Regional College by U.S. News & World Report for thirteen consecutive years and named a College of Distinction for nine consecutive years, Dean serves approximately 1,200 full-time students and 400 part-time students and offers more than 50 combined bachelor's and associate degree programs and specializations, as well as a robust schedule of continuing studies and certificate programs throughout the year. Dean College is perfectly situated in Franklin, Massachusetts, which is conveniently located between Boston and Providence, Rhode Island, and is accessible to Boston by commuter rail. The Dean College/Franklin rail station is only a five-minute walk from campus. Approximately 90 percent of the College's student population lives on campus and Dean provides a supportive academic environment that thrives on hands-on engagement and exceptional teaching. This community-wide commitment of always going the extra mile for students is known as The Dean Difference. Outside of the classroom, students participate in 16 athletic teams and more than 40 on-campus groups and organizations. Ninety-six percent of our bachelor's degree students are employed or enrolled in graduate school within 12 months of graduation. Alumni are hard at work in top-ranked graduate programs and are employed by organizations such as Universal Studios, Dell Technologies, Liberty Mutual, Kraft Sports + Entertainment, the Boston Ballet, and more. What is The Dean Difference ? The Dean Difference isn't any one thing. It's not a program or a professor. It's not a single class or a club. It's the way our academic support networks and community overlap, interweave, and magnify each other. Our difference unites us. It's our secret formula. It's the nucleus around which we orbit. It isn't one thing, it's everything. Job Description: Dean College invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice, a 10-month, full-time faculty position. The School of Liberal Arts and Sciences is looking for an accomplished educator with experience teaching criminal justice coursework who focuses on experiential learning and active engagement in their classroom. This person will collaborate with the program coordinator and other full-time and adjunct faculty in the program to provide students with the needed background, knowledge and rich experiences that prepares them for work in various industry settings or in graduate school. All Dean College academic programs are grounded in the liberal arts, stress experiential learning, and seek to develop a career mindset, with the Dean Career Advantage (DCA), in its students to prepare them for life after Dean. Applications may be considered until the position is filled. Priority will be given to applications received by October 1, 2026. Expected salary range: $69,000-$72,000 when annualized, commensurate with experience. The College also offers a comprehensive benefits package, including health insurance, retirement contributions, and generous paid time off. Position responsibilities include: Teach 15 contact hours/semester; 5:5 teaching load. The ability and willingness to teach across a wide variety of criminal justice courses, from the introductory course to upper-division requirements. Develop curriculum grounded in best practices and assess the results of program initiatives. Coach and mentor students regarding academic and career goals including graduate school preparation. Participate in committees as assigned, attend school and program meetings. Participate in recruitment activities and student orientations. Hold office hours as required and meet with students by appointment. Engage with the school and college community. There is no faculty advising load. Students are served by a professional advising staff. Other duties as required or assigned. Requirements: Master's degree in criminal justice or related discipline is required; A PhD (terminal degree) in Criminal Justice or related discipline is desired. The area of specialization is open within criminology and criminal justice. Undergraduate teaching experience, including leading students in class projects and practical applications, is required. Experience with online teaching is preferred. Demonstrated experience with program development, management, and assessment. Demonstrated experience in curriculum development and innovative classroom pedagogy. Demonstrated success teaching a diverse population of undergraduates at varying stages of academic readiness. Experience with course management systems (i.e. Canvas), digital technology, Microsoft Office Suite (e.g. Teams, Word, PowerPoint) and classroom media such as digital whiteboards is desired. Additional Information: Dean College is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate against applicants or employees on the basis of race, color, religion, religious creed, national or ethnic origin, ancestry, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, or any other status protected by applicable law. This commitment applies to all employment practices, including recruitment, hiring, promotion, compensation, benefits, professional development, continuation of employment, and other terms and conditions of employment. The College prohibits discrimination, harassment, and retaliation in violation of applicable law or College policy. Dean College is committed to maintaining a welcoming and respectful workplace and to providing equal opportunity to all qualified applicants and employees. Application Instructions: Please submit your Resume/CV, Cover Letter, all unofficial transcripts; and contact information of three references. (PLEASE NOTE: Applications that are incomplete will not be considered). Note: After submitting your resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your Cover Letter and any additional documents. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Dean College Careers Account to check your completed application or upload additional documents. URL: www.dean.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Dean College 99 Main Street, Franklin MA 02038"
    },
    "https://dean.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205528": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of English",
      "description": "Dean College\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor of English Dean College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor of English Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor of English Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Liberal Arts and Sciences Locations: Franklin, MA Posted: Oct 6, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-Time Academic Year Position ID: 205528 Share About Dean College: Dean College is a private, residential New England college grounded in a culture and tradition that all students deserve the opportunity to discover and exceed their greatest aspirations. A personal and transformative community since 1865, Dean tirelessly inspires our students to unimagined heights through personalized support and integrated delivery of academic, co-curricular, and experiential learning. Our graduates are lifelong learners who thrive in their careers, embrace social responsibility, and demonstrate leadership. Recognized as a Top Regional College by U.S. News & World Report for fifteenth consecutive years and named a College of Distinction for eleven consecutive years, Dean serves more than 1,000 full-time students and offers over 50 academic programs and specializations, as well as a robust schedule of continuing studies and certificate programs throughout the year. Dean College is perfectly situated in Franklin, Massachusetts, which is conveniently located between Boston and Providence, Rhode Island, and is accessible to Boston by commuter rail. The Dean College/Franklin rail station is only a five-minute walk from campus. Approximately 90 percent of the College's student population lives on campus and Dean provides a supportive academic environment that thrives on hands-on engagement and exceptional teaching. This community-wide commitment of always going the extra mile for students is known as The Dean Difference. Outside of the classroom, students participate in 16 athletic teams and more than 40 on-campus groups and organizations. Ninety-six percent of our bachelor's degree students are employed or enrolled in graduate school within 12 months of graduation. Alumni are hard at work in top-ranked graduate programs and are employed by organizations such as Universal Studios, Dell Technologies, Liberty Mutual, Kraft Sports + Entertainment, the Boston Ballet, and more. What is The Dean Difference? The Dean Difference isn't any one thing. It's not a program or a professor. It's not a single class or a club. It's the way our academic support networks and community overlap, interweave, and magnify each other. Our difference unites us. It's our secret formula. It's the nucleus around which we orbit. It isn't one thing, it's everything. Job Description: The School of Liberal Arts and Sciences is looking for a dynamic, experienced, student-centered educator to join the English faculty within our interdisciplinary Humanities Department, who will be an integral member of the English major, its Film Studies Track, and our innovative Content Creation and Influencing major. Dean College invites applications for this full-time, 10-month, annually renewable Assistant Professor position. We seek an accomplished educator with experience teaching media and film theory, as well as thematic courses in literature, film, and/or pop culture studies (all specializations welcome). Experience teaching digital storytelling would be a plus. This educator should be well versed in creating a classroom environment based on experiential learning and active engagement. The courses this position will teach also include Composition I (ENG 111) and Composition II (ENG 112). A collaborative, effective working relationship with Humanities faculty, first-year writing faculty, and Communications faculty will be essential. Applications may be considered until the position is filled; however, first consideration will be given to those applicants received by December 1, 2026. Expected salary range: $69,000-$72,000 when annualized, commensurate with experience. The College also offers a comprehensive benefits package, including health insurance, retirement contributions, and generous paid time off. Position responsibilities include: Teach a 5:5 teaching load (teaching 15 contact hours/semester); There is no faculty advising load. Students are served by a professional advising staff; Coach and mentor students regarding academic and career goals including graduate school preparation; Develop curriculum grounded in best practices and assess the results of program initiatives; Hold office hours as required and meet with students by appointment; Participate in committees as assigned, attend school and program meetings; Participate in recruitment activities and student orientations; Other duties as assigned. Requirements: PhD in Film Studies, Media Studies, English, or related areas in the Humanities is required; Candidates with an ABD will be considered. Undergraduate teaching experience is required, particularly with first-year undergraduates. Commitment to undergraduate liberal arts education and a demonstrated ability to work effectively with faculty, students, and staff from diverse backgrounds. Strong computer skills, the use of technologies and/or strategies to enhance pedagogy, the ability to access the College's online resources, and a willingness to be responsive to students via digital tools, including our digital learning management system. The successful candidate will possess expertise in learner-centered teaching and will have the ability to work effectively with a culturally diverse student body with a variety of learning styles and at varying stages of academic readiness. Experience with online teaching, course management systems, digital technology, and classroom media such as smart boards is desired. Additional Information: Dean College is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate against applicants or employees on the basis of race, color, religion, religious creed, national or ethnic origin, ancestry, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, or any other status protected by applicable law. This commitment applies to all employment practices, including recruitment, hiring, promotion, compensation, benefits, professional development, continuation of employment, and other terms and conditions of employment. The College prohibits discrimination, harassment, and retaliation in violation of applicable law or College policy. Dean College is committed to maintaining a welcoming and respectful workplace and to providing equal opportunity to all qualified applicants and employees. Application Instructions: Please submit your Resume/CV, Cover Letter, all unofficial transcripts; and contact information of three references. (PLEASE NOTE: Applications that are incomplete will not be considered). Note: After submitting your resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your Cover Letter and any additional documents. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Dean College Careers Account to check your completed application or upload additional documents. URL: www.dean.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Dean College 99 Main Street, Franklin MA 02038"
    },
    "https://dean.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205833": {
      "title": "Associate Registrar",
      "description": "Dean College\nJob Posting: Associate Registrar Dean College \n\tJob Posting: Associate Registrar Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Associate Registrar Category: Administration/Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Registrar's Office Locations: Franklin, MA Posted: Oct 15, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-Time Fiscal Year Position ID: 205833 Share About Dean College: Dean College is a private, residential New England college grounded in a culture and tradition that all students deserve the opportunity to discover and exceed their greatest aspirations. A personal and transformative community since 1865, Dean tirelessly inspires our students to unimagined heights through personalized support and integrated delivery of academic, co-curricular, and experiential learning. Our graduates are lifelong learners who thrive in their careers, embrace social responsibility, and demonstrate leadership. Recognized as a Top Regional College by U.S. News & World Report for fifteenth consecutive years and named a College of Distinction for eleven consecutive years, Dean serves more than 1,000 full-time students and offers over 50 academic programs and specializations, as well as a robust schedule of continuing studies and certificate programs throughout the year. Dean College is perfectly situated in Franklin, Massachusetts, which is conveniently located between Boston and Providence, Rhode Island, and is accessible to Boston by commuter rail. The Dean College/Franklin rail station is only a five-minute walk from campus. Approximately 90 percent of the College's student population lives on campus and Dean provides a supportive academic environment that thrives on hands-on engagement and exceptional teaching. This community-wide commitment of always going the extra mile for students is known as The Dean Difference. Outside of the classroom, students participate in 16 athletic teams and more than 40 on-campus groups and organizations. Ninety-six percent of our bachelor's degree students are employed or enrolled in graduate school within 12 months of graduation. Alumni are hard at work in top-ranked graduate programs and are employed by organizations such as Universal Studios, Dell Technologies, Liberty Mutual, Kraft Sports + Entertainment, the Boston Ballet, and more. What is The Dean Difference? The Dean Difference isn't any one thing. It's not a program or a professor. It's not a single class or a club. It's the way our academic support networks and community overlap, interweave, and magnify each other. Our difference unites us. It's our secret formula. It's the nucleus around which we orbit. It isn't one thing, it's everything. Job Description: Dean College invites applications for the position of Associate Registrar within the Office of the Registrar. The Office of the Registrar is responsible for the maintenance of student records and works to improve the student, faculty, and staff experience at Dean College. The Associate Registrar is primarily responsible for maintaining academic and curriculum information as well as overseeing the start and end of semester/year processes.  In addition, this position uses various software applications to provide reporting support for internal and external agencies and to assist with managing daily operations. This position works closely with the Registrar and assists with strategic and operational functions.  As a partner with other campus departments, the Associate Registrar works collaboratively with Academic Affairs, Admissions, Student Financial Services, and Success and Career Advisors to maintain accurate and reliable student records. Expected salary range: $67,000-$72,000 per year, commensurate with experience. The College also offers a comprehensive benefits package, including health insurance, retirement contributions, and generous paid time off. Position responsibilities include: Maintain systems that provide academic information for current students, including Degree Audit and Docuware. Update annual changes to student completion dates, process waivers and substitutions, and update academic programs' degree audits based on catalog content and updates. Oversee graduation tasks, including updating the graduation application, conducting mid-year and final audits for all students, and tracking and reporting any missing requirements to Success & Career Advisors. Coordinate diploma production and delivery and assist with the Commencement ceremony program, reader's list, and other reports as requested. Manage tasks associated with the readmission process, start-of-semester check in processes, grading processes, Honor Societies coding, and student withdrawal reporting. Work with Athletics & Recreation to manage student-athlete information and generate reports to support compliance requirements. Assist with Academic Standing review and calculate Dean's list and President's List. Verify calculations are correct and communicate outcomes to the campus community. Support the Registrar by ensuring all office personnel are cross-trained on internal and external data mining/reporting, including course demand, classroom space needs, and transfer credit equivalencies. Serve as back up for reporting to the National Student Clearinghouse, Department of Veteran Affairs, IPEDS, public surveys, and internal data groups. Represent the Registrar's Office as a member on various College-wide committees, such as the Commencement team, the academic calendar building work team, and the Opening Committee. Collaborate with Admissions, the Advising Center, and Student Financial Services to monitor student information, ensuring record accuracy, data integrity, and compliance with federal regulations, particularly FERPA. Conduct annual reviews of processes and procedures to enhance office efficiency and accuracy, ensuring that documentation is consistently created and maintained. Other duties and projects as assigned or required. Requirements: Bachelor's degree required; master's degree preferred. 3-5 years' experience working in a higher education environment or similar field. Familiarity with Ellucian Colleague or comparable ERP system, as well as eTranscript providers is preferred. Knowledge of U.S. educational systems, credentials, and Family Education Rights and Privacy (FERPA) The ideal candidate is highly detail-oriented with excellent communication skills, capable of efficiently managing multiple projects, and proficient in Microsoft Office, particularly Excel and Word. Must be able to work independently and demonstrate strong analytical, organizational, and customer service skills. Additional Information: Dean College is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate against applicants or employees on the basis of race, color, religion, religious creed, national or ethnic origin, ancestry, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, or any other status protected by applicable law. This commitment applies to all employment practices, including recruitment, hiring, promotion, compensation, benefits, professional development, continuation of employment, and other terms and conditions of employment. The College prohibits discrimination, harassment, and retaliation in violation of applicable law or College policy. Dean College is committed to maintaining a welcoming and respectful workplace and to providing equal opportunity to all qualified applicants and employees. Application Instructions: Please submit your Resume/CV, Cover Letter, all unofficial transcripts; and contact information of three references. (PLEASE NOTE: Applications that are incomplete will not be considered). Note: After submitting your resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your Cover Letter and any additional documents. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Dean College Careers Account to check your completed application or upload additional documents. URL: www.dean.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Dean College 99 Main Street, Franklin MA 02038"
    },
    "https://dean.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205915": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Student Engagement",
      "description": "Dean College\nJob Posting: Assistant Director of Student Engagement Dean College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Director of Student Engagement Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Director of Student Engagement Category: Administration/Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Student Activities & Leadership Development Locations: Franklin, MA Posted: Oct 19, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-Time Fiscal Year Position ID: 205915 Share About Dean College: Dean College is a private, residential New England college grounded in a culture and tradition that all students deserve the opportunity to discover and exceed their greatest aspirations. A personal and transformative community since 1865, Dean tirelessly inspires our students to unimagined heights through personalized support and integrated delivery of academic, co-curricular, and experiential learning. Our graduates are lifelong learners who thrive in their careers, embrace social responsibility, and demonstrate leadership. Recognized as a Top Regional College by U.S. News & World Report for fifteenth consecutive years and named a College of Distinction for eleven consecutive years, Dean serves more than 1,000 full-time students and offers over 50 academic programs and specializations, as well as a robust schedule of continuing studies and certificate programs throughout the year. Dean College is perfectly situated in Franklin, Massachusetts, which is conveniently located between Boston and Providence, Rhode Island, and is accessible to Boston by commuter rail. The Dean College/Franklin rail station is only a five-minute walk from campus. Approximately 90 percent of the College's student population lives on campus and Dean provides a supportive academic environment that thrives on hands-on engagement and exceptional teaching. This community-wide commitment of always going the extra mile for students is known as The Dean Difference. Outside of the classroom, students participate in 16 athletic teams and more than 40 on-campus groups and organizations. Ninety-six percent of our bachelor's degree students are employed or enrolled in graduate school within 12 months of graduation. Alumni are hard at work in top-ranked graduate programs and are employed by organizations such as Universal Studios, Dell Technologies, Liberty Mutual, Kraft Sports + Entertainment, the Boston Ballet, and more. What is The Dean Difference? The Dean Difference isn't any one thing. It's not a program or a professor. It's not a single class or a club. It's the way our academic support networks and community overlap, interweave, and magnify each other. Our difference unites us. It's our secret formula. It's the nucleus around which we orbit. It isn't one thing, it's everything. Job Description: The Assistant Director of Student Engagement plays an integral role in creating meaningful opportunities for students to connect, get involved, and develop as leaders. The position advises the Dean Activities Board, supports the development and administration of student organizations, leads the recruitment and development of Orientation Leaders, and creates programming that responds to the needs and interests of the student community, including commuter students. The Assistant Director collaborates with campus partners on events and initiatives and works with the Director to advance a comprehensive student engagement program that strengthens involvement, leadership, connection, and sense of community. Expected salary range: $55,000-$58,000 per year, commensurate with experience. The College also offers a comprehensive benefits package, including health insurance, retirement contributions, and generous paid time off. The position includes a live-on requirement. The Assistant Director will be provided with an unfurnished campus house adjacent to campus. Utilities are included, and a meal plan is provided when the dining center is open. Position responsibilities include: Advise the Dean Activities Board (DAB) and provide leadership and guidance in the development, coordination, and delivery of signature student programs and traditions, including Winter Week and Spring Week. Direct the recognition and ongoing administration of student organizations, providing guidance to student leaders and advisors on college policies, organizational operations, event planning, recruitment, and member engagement. Lead the recruitment, selection, hiring, training, supervision, assessment, and ongoing development of Orientation Leaders who support New Student Orientation and Bulldog Beginnings. Develop and coordinate programming specifically for commuter students, incorporating student feedback to address their interests, needs, and opportunities for meaningful campus involvement. Collaborate with campus partners in the planning and implementation of student programs and activities, supporting communication, logistics, and successful execution. With the Director, develop and implement a comprehensive student activities program that promotes student involvement, leadership development, connection, and a strong sense of community. Serve as a campus resource on student activities, organizations, and engagement initiatives, providing guidance and connecting students with appropriate resources and opportunities. Coordinate the Office's participation in Admissions and enrollment events, including the development of displays, information tables, activities, and other programming that highlights the Office's programs and services for prospective and admitted students. Lead, coordinate, or support Office programs, initiatives, and events, as assigned, including direct responsibility for designated areas of the Office's programming. Serve on College committees and working groups and participate in institutional initiatives as assigned. Other duties as assigned/required. Managerial and supervisory responsibilities: New Student Orientation Leaders Office Work Study Requirements: Master's degree in Higher Education, Student Affairs, College Student Personnel, Counseling, or a related field preferred; bachelor's degree required. Minimum of two years of professional experience in higher education or student affairs, with relevant experience in student activities, programming, orientation, or student engagement. Experience developing, implementing, assessing, and continuously improving student programs, activities, and initiatives. Background in advising and supporting student organizations, student leaders, and/or student programming boards. Experience recruiting, training, supervising, and evaluating student employees or student leaders. Knowledge of student development, leadership development, student engagement, orientation and transition programming. Demonstrated ability to build collaborative relationships and work effectively with students, faculty, staff, and campus partners. Strong organizational, project management, communication, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and initiatives in a dynamic environment. Commitment to fostering an inclusive campus community and creating meaningful opportunities for students to connect, engage, and develop as leaders. Ability to reside on campus and maintain availability for programs and activities outside of traditional business hours. Must be available to work nights and weekends. Additional Information: Dean College is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate against applicants or employees on the basis of race, color, religion, religious creed, national or ethnic origin, ancestry, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, or any other status protected by applicable law. This commitment applies to all employment practices, including recruitment, hiring, promotion, compensation, benefits, professional development, continuation of employment, and other terms and conditions of employment. The College prohibits discrimination, harassment, and retaliation in violation of applicable law or College policy. Dean College is committed to maintaining a welcoming and respectful workplace and to providing equal opportunity to all qualified applicants and employees. Application Instructions: Please submit your Resume/CV, Cover Letter, all unofficial transcripts; and contact information of three references. (PLEASE NOTE: Applications that are incomplete will not be considered). Note: After submitting your resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your Cover Letter and any additional documents. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Dean College Careers Account to check your completed application or upload additional documents. URL: www.dean.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Dean College 99 Main Street, Franklin MA 02038"
    }
